From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] NsisTarget: extract uninstaller without wine on Linux

Stock electron-builder 26.8.1 runs the intermediate installer under wine on
non-Windows hosts to slice out the embedded uninstaller (`execWine` in the
else branch below). That is the only hard wine dependency when building a
Windows NSIS package on Linux.

electron-builder already ships a pure-Node extractor (UninstallerReader:
parses the PE + NSIS byte stream), but enables it only on macOS Catalina+.
Loosen that condition to every non-Windows host: the two-pass makensis flow
is preserved and no exe is executed during uninstaller extraction.

NOTE: patch 001 pins electron-builder to exactly 26.8.1 because the hunk
context below drifts between app-builder-lib versions. If you ever install
a different version, re-generate the context (the semantic change is the
single `if` line).

NOT NEEDED when restoring node_modules from the committed snapshot:
  vendor/desktop-node-modules/restore.sh
ships the tree with this patch PRE-APPLIED. Only the plain `npm install`
path needs this patch, applied AFTER install (any reinstall overwrites it —
build scripts must re-apply and verify, see repack/build-repack.sh):
  desktop/node_modules/app-builder-lib/out/targets/nsis/NsisTarget.js

Verify: grep -q 'process.platform !== "win32"' <file>

--- a/desktop/node_modules/app-builder-lib/out/targets/nsis/NsisTarget.js
+++ b/desktop/node_modules/app-builder-lib/out/targets/nsis/NsisTarget.js
@@ -350,7 +350,7 @@ class NsisTarget extends builder_util_1.Archiver {
         defines.UNINSTALLER_OUT_FILE = isWin ? uninstallerPath : path.win32.join("Z:", uninstallerPath);
         await this.executeMakensis(defines, commands, sharedHeader + (await this.computeFinalScript(script, false, archs)));
         // http://forums.winamp.com/showthread.php?p=3078545
-        if ((0, macosVersion_1.isMacOsCatalina)()) {
+        if (process.platform !== "win32") {
             try {
                 await nsisUtil_1.UninstallerReader.exec(installerPath, uninstallerPath);
             }
